.TH SUPIVPN 8 "October 2026" "SupiVPN" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
supivpn \- authorize OpenVPN sessions through SupiVPN
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B supivpn
.BI \-config " file"
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the VPN node agent. The Debian service uses
/etc/supivpn/node/agent.json and starts its paired OpenVPN service after
the agent binds its listeners. A service readiness notification does not
replace the HTTPS /readyz check for management and lease readiness.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " file"
Read JSON configuration. The standalone default is /etc/supivpn/config.json.
.TP
.B \-check-config
Validate configuration without starting services.
.TP
.B \-operator-request
Read a local user-session request from standard input and send it to the
operator socket selected by the configuration. Requires local authorization.
.TP
.B \-learn-address
Validate the source address supplied by the OpenVPN learn-address hook.
This mode is intended for invocation by OpenVPN.
.TP
.BI \-route-device " device"
TUN interface used by the shared UDP/TCP pool hooks. Requires \-route-network.
.TP
.BI \-route-network " CIDR"
Private VPN network for per-client host routes. With \-learn-address, validates
and installs only the assigned client address using fixed iproute2 commands.
.TP
.B \-route-disconnect
Remove this client's shared-pool route on OpenVPN disconnect.
Use only with explicit \-route-device and \-route-network.
.TP
.BI \-verify-profile-metadata " required|legacy"
Validate authenticated tls-crypt-v2 metadata for the selected listener format.
Intended for OpenVPN's tls-crypt-v2-verify hook; starts no services.
Legacy mode accepts historical unbound keys only. It also requires an explicit
legacy agent and controller node allowlist, and will be removed in v0.10.0.
.TP
.BI \-profile-max-age " duration"
Optional maximum key age for the metadata hook, such as 2160h.
The default zero does not impose an age limit.
.TP
.B \-h
Show command-line help.
.SH FILES
/usr/share/doc/supivpn-node/examples/agent.example.json
.br
/usr/share/doc/supivpn-node/DEBIAN_PACKAGING.md.gz
.SH NOTES
Use supivpn-node.service to start, stop or restart the node and its transports.
TCP is disabled by default. See TRANSPORTS.md for configuration.
Installation never activates a VPN or modifies host networking.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR supivpn-controller (8),
.BR supivpn-profile (8),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR openvpn (8)
